  <description>
    <p>
      Dóru is local-first genealogy for the AI era. A project is a single
      .doru file (SQLite) with photos in a media folder next to it — nothing
      is hidden, nothing is uploaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your family tree lives on your disk and works fully offline. Back up by
      copying a folder; open it on macOS, Linux, or Windows.
    </p>
    <p>
      AI-native: agent chat with tree tools, a built-in MCP server for Claude
      Desktop and Cursor, an MCP host for external servers, and ACP agents.
    </p>
    <p>
      Private by design: no accounts, no cloud, no telemetry. The only network
      calls are the AI providers and MCP servers you configure yourself — API
      keys stay in your OS keychain, and with Ollama or LM Studio even the AI
      runs entirely on your machine.
    </p>
    <p>
      Settings and themes are plain text files that hot-reload, GEDCOM import
      and export keep you interoperable, and the interface is localized in 17
      languages. Dóru is free and open source (MIT).
    </p>
  </description>

